CRANEWARE: WHEN A HEALTHCARE SOFTWARE VENDOR BECOMES A CONCENTRATION-RISK NODE

Subhead:

No hospital outage was required for this to matter. A vendor embedded across thousands of healthcare organizations can become an intelligence and supply-chain target even when customer-facing services stay online.

IG-2026-049 — Craneware

InfinityGrid Classification: HIGH, potentially CRITICAL depending on final data scope
Sector: Healthcare Software / Revenue Cycle / 340B
Region: United States / United Kingdom
Incident Type: Unauthorized access / data exfiltration
Affected Environment: Subset of Craneware data environment
Threat Actor: Unknown
Initial Access: Not publicly disclosed
Known CVE: None publicly established
Data Volume: Not quantified publicly
Operational Disruption: None reported
Regulators / Authorities: FBI and UK ICO notified
Primary Failure Domain: Undisclosed
Primary Risk Theme: Healthcare software concentration / third-party data exposure

Craneware says its platform supports financial and operational functions in healthcare and markets its Trisus platform as a Microsoft Azure-based cloud platform. The company works with more than 2,000 hospitals and health systems and nearly 10,000 clinics and pharmacies, according to current company descriptions and reporting.
